From 3d9916b2dc041cd1bd112f146b5465a19df19d4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:56:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(routing): resume on the allocation store's route, not a
 lagging model_config copy [daveey]

MacBook chat 20261026_205117_f67f0d sat on an unanswered kanban notice (unresolved{notice_tail}) for 7 h:
every agent build for it (notice close-out wake, kanban sweep wake, chat-closeout, automation replay) failed
with "Exact pinned route cannot fail over".

Why-chain (evidence: state.db sessions row, model-routing.sqlite3 routes row, agent.log 11:33-18:41 PT):
1. Why did no turn answer the notice? Each wake's agent build raised ModelRoutingError (agent.log, 20+ lines).
2. Why? Resume pinned claude-opus-5-5/anthropic, but the allocation store holds an exact pin on
   gpt-6-astra/openai-codex (reason explicit-switch), and an exact pin cannot fail over.
3. Why did resume pick claude? restore_route reads model_config.model_routing, which still recorded the
   pre-switch claude allocation; the row's model (gpt-6-astra) disagreed and e320c9d273 made "the record wins".
4. Why was the record stale? model_config.model_routing is a copy rewritten only after a turn; the honoured
   switch moved the store without a completed turn rewriting the copy.
5. Why wasn't it caught? e320c9d273's tests assumed the copy and the store agree; no test had the store moved
   by an explicit switch while the copy lagged.

Fix: restore_route takes the session id and prefers the allocation store's row for that lineage and class
(RoutingState.peek), falling back to the copy only when the store has none. All four resume paths pass the id
(Desktop/tui agent_factory, CLI, gateway restart, API server). Policy still gates the restored pin.
Tests: store-vs-copy unit tests next to the desync tests, plus one test per entry path.
